   REVERSE ENGINEERING NOTES
 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
   项目J is a Chinese desktop document generator built with E-language (EPL)
   statically compiled, rendering its UI through miniblink (Chromium), with
   MS ScriptControl + JScript9Legacy for template scripting.

   License enforcement is ONLINE (card key), but the FINAL DECISION is made
   LOCALLY by the client:

     1. Authorization channel (observed)
        Plain TCP to <AUTH-SRV>:4001, custom binary protocol:
          REQ : E8 03 00 00 | CB 02 00 00 | <715 bytes ciphertext>
                (cmd = 1000, payload length = 715)
          RESP: 01 02 04 02 05 04 | 1C 00 00 00 | <18 bytes ciphertext>
                (magic 6B, total length 28)
        No TLS, no transport integrity. The error string shown to the user
        ("卡号不存在") does NOT exist anywhere in the local image (verified by
        GBK + UTF-16LE full-image search) -> it is delivered by the server.

     2. Why static patching is impossible
        The .ev3n section has rawsize = 0 on disk; the code only exists after
        the packer decrypts it at runtime. Whole-file entropy ~= 7.997/64KB.
        Therefore NO file-level patch exists - only runtime memory patching.

     3. Why runtime patching IS possible (key insight)
        DllCharacteristics = 0x0000  -> no ASLR, ImageBase fixed at 0x400000
        .ev3n section    = RWX      -> writable and executable at runtime
        No anti-tamper, no self-check, no VM virtualization.
        => An external process can simply WriteProcessMemory the auth branch.

     4. The local decision point (CWE-602)
        0x00401290  83 7D FC 00        cmp  dword ptr [ebp-4], 0
        0x00401294  0F 84 4D 02 00 00  je   0x004014E7      ; ==0 -> DENIED
        A single 6-byte conditional jump decides the whole license outcome.

     5. Heartbeat re-check (must also be neutralized)
        Function 0x0041AB86 re-queries the server and, on failure, makes the
        CLIENT terminate itself (not a server-side revocation):
          0x0041AC81  0F 8D 34 01 00 00   jge 0x0041ADBB
          0x0041AE05  0F 8D 34 01 00 00   jge 0x0041AF3F

